1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,457
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,040
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,800
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:29,457
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting.

11
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,377
Either way, I'm feeling alive!

12
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,860
Look out below.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,120
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,397
Raise your flag up high.

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,040
Hail a brand new dawn.

16
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,837
Blaze across the sky.

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,837
Time to journey on.

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,317
On your mark.

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,217
Camel of other things.

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,097
We're on Earth, a legendary!

21
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:54,017
Hooray!

22
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,580
If you can show your breath,
Then we'll make some waves.

23
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:00,377
We run our daunted.

24
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,617
Ain't no beginners.

25
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,357
Cause if you're wanted,
Then you're a winner.

26
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,860
For we are on the cruise,
And freedom is the only rule.

27
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:12,277
Fearless night and day.

28
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,140
Cause that's just our way.

29
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,197
Find one piece.

30
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,537
I'll be the first.

31
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,797
I'll put it be so bad.

32
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,710
Just a bit first.

33
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:22,137
It's all this real.

34
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,360
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel.

35
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,437
I'm done playing, filled with the waiting.

36
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:33,137
In a world I'm feeling
alive, but I'll be loud.

37
00:01:33,220 --> 00:01:37,040
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

38
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far.

39
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,320
Gotta make it to the end.

40
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,677
Whatever danger we find,
no one ever left behind!

41
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,780
I've always got your back, my friend.

42
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward.

43
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,117
Dreaming from the very
first day I'd make my name.

44
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,120
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed?

45
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave.

46
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,277
In every world I'm feeling alive.

47
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,577
Look out below.

48
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:12,980
Wake up, sunshine.

49
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:17,120
Wake up, sunshine.

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,177
Wake up, sunshine.

51
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:23,620
And here we go!

52
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:28,300
We go!

53
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,240
Move it!

54
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,760
Please! Stop him!

55
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,901
He's getting away with our money!

56
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,720
Somebody do something!

57
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,600
Just stay out of my way, got it?

58
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:55,466
Because you don't want to see what I'll
do to this girl if you try to be a hero.

59
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,480
Your Majesty.

60
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,517
Wait, don't go that way!

61
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,357
You shouldn't involve
yourself with such a thing.

62
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,780
This is not our responsibility.

63
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,010
Please wait!

64
00:03:11,093 --> 00:03:12,020
Queen Otohime.

65
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:15,480
Who's that?

66
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,700
Don't come any closer, I'll shoot!

67
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,560
I warned you!

68
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:33,780
I missed?

69
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,560
Dammit, goodbye!

70
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,240
I got you!

71
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:05,260
Wait, isn't that Queen Otohime?

72
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:09,617
My hair!

73
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,600
Hurry, doctor!

74
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,360
Your highness, let me take a look.

75
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,240
It's fractured, I'm afraid.

76
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,697
She hit him once and broke her hand?

77
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:20,680
It's fine.

78
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,000
Queen Otohime!

79
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,880
The queen?

80
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:32,897
Why would you do something as foolish and
selfish as robbing your fellow people?

81
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:33,937
What do you care?

82
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:36,357
Like a rich member of the
royal family could understand.

83
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:41,028
I got ten kids waiting at home, and all
they do is cry because they're hungry!

84
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,200
All the more reason!

85
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,060
No! Queen Otohime!

86
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,397
You must stop hitting him, please!

87
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,597
They're much too delicate.

88
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,637
You will only make your injury worse!

89
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:55,560
I don't care!

90
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,320
I have to do this!

91
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:01,580
Even if my hand must shatter to
pieces, he will learn his lesson!

92
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:09,337
Do you think your children would
be happy if they knew the truth?

93
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:11,655
If they knew their father was a thief?

94
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:15,918
You should be trying to live your
life in a way that makes them proud.

95
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:23,660
However, I owe you an apology.

96
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:25,780
Please forgive me.

97
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,408
Even though I'm your queen,

98
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,177
I've been completely
ignorant to the hardships

99
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:35,201
that one of my subjects
has been forced to endure.

100
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:38,220
My heart can't take it.

101
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:42,420
Your worries and your
pain, they're killing me.

102
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,980
You must have had a reason for doing this.

103
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,120
I don't know.

104
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,140
It's not that I wanted to.

105
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:56,820
But I, I felt like there was no other way.

106
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:01,600
Somebody sent fire to my
store and stole all my money.

107
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,477
We couldn't save anything
before we hurt down.

108
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:07,140
Just like that, I didn't have a job.

109
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,900
My debts started piling up,
and now my kids are starving.

110
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,377
I'm sorry that happened.

111
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:15,600
And I understand.

112
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,560
I really do, but...

113
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:18,950
It's wrong!

114
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:23,777
If you do to others what was done
to you, the cycle will never end!

115
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:24,690
I'm sorry!

116
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,880
No, I'm sorry.

117
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:31,697
We weren't there for you in your time of
need, so that makes us accountable as well.

118
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:32,680
Your Highness,

119
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:37,257
it's really not your fault, but that's a
terribly generous thing for you to say.

120
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:38,811
It's still wrong, though!

121
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,280
I know, I know!

122
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:41,740
Then don't do it!

123
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,840
You've changed me, and my whole life!

124
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:48,372
Thank you so much, after seeing
how much you cried for me!

125
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:50,220
I'll never steal again!

126
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,637
I know that you won't!

127
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,308
Best of luck in the future!

128
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,357
We're so lucky to have a member
of the royal family who's

129
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,357
not afraid to share the troubles
of common people like us.

130
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,557
She nearly had me crying along with her,

131
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:04,217
though I certainly hope she
doesn't break her hand next time.

132
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:08,380
Our Queen Otohime is a one-of-a-kind
ruler, I can tell you that much.

133
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,080
She has such a kind heart.

134
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:11,320
And look there!

135
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,777
Even the children of
the kingdom adore her.

136
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:14,900
Queen Otohime!

137
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:20,215
I'll do everything I can to
protect your smiling faces.

138
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:24,400
Your nose is running terribly!

139
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,171
If I don't reprimand you for it, who will?

140
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:31,327
You look ridiculous with mucus
dribbling out of just one side.

141
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,541
It's more dignified to
dribble from both nostrils.

142
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,660
Such a tender moment!

143
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,380
I guess so.

144
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,680
No one was more passionate or loving.

145
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,854
Every day, Queen Otohime descended
from the palace to address the nation.

146
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,769
That day was no different.

147
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:56,498
The time has come for us to relocate
the Ryugu kingdom to the surface.

148
00:07:56,780 --> 00:08:00,309
Our skins are different colors,
and we do not look the same.

149
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:02,997
These are the things the
humans say in order to

150
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,897
avoid understanding us and
our unique way of life.

151
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:09,274
But that's why we should move,
to understand each other.

152
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:12,377
Our worlds are 10,000 meters apart,

153
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:16,080
so that is also the distance
between our ways of thinking.

154
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,820
I know you're afraid.

155
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:26,696
After all, the humans who come to
our island are pirates and criminals.

156
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,277
And the humans who buy our people from

157
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:32,177
kidnappers like them are
cruel and Corrupt nobles

158
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:35,417
it's true that our only exposure to humans

159
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,257
has been negative but That doesn't mean we

160
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:41,117
can judge all humans the same I believe in

161
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,937
my heart That there are
good ones among them

162
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:46,577
as well and thus to
improve relations we Must

163
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:51,877
move our kingdom to be
under the same Sun it

164
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:56,657
is my goal to express our Intention to
relocate above sea level at this year's world

165
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:59,357
summit but in order to
do that I Need all of

166
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:05,297
you to sign while uh I

167
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:06,417
admit it sounds like a

168
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:09,057
good idea in theory
but just the thought Of

169
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,357
living near humans is

170
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:16,677
well I understand how

171
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,137
you feel however this
is our chance to make

172
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:21,926
a Real change rather
than suffering in silence

173
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,917
Please look I'm

174
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:32,837
sorry but no it's no

175
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:36,540
use History can't be fought so easily

176
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,560
Hello everyone, I'm home!

177
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:57,460
I'm home, Shirahoshi!

178
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,237
I hope you can forgive me, darling.

179
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:12,640
Mommy didn't mean to be so late!

180
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:19,937
Even with your nose running on
one side, you're still beautiful.

181
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:24,177
We stayed with her the entire time you
were gone so she'd feel safe, Mother.

182
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,037
It's true, Mother, we did?

183
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,760
I have such brave sons.

184
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,064
But what happened to your hand?

185
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,320
Are you okay?

186
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,577
Oh, don't worry, dear.

187
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:34,490
It's nothing.

188
00:10:34,573 --> 00:10:35,403
See?

189
00:10:35,486 --> 00:10:38,800
To ensure you all have a
bright future, I would suffer.

190
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,460
So much worse than this.

191
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,420
If Queen Otohime wants
to make announcements,

192
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:50,637
she really should do them by video
rather than going down there in person.

193
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:53,955
Unfortunately, thanks to
her strong observation Haki,

194
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,917
Doing something like that would
go against her very nature.

195
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:01,397
She would rather win the hearts of the
citizens in person than from the palace.

196
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:04,180
It's one of Otohime's guiding principles.

197
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,188
Not even I can change that.

198
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:08,957
She's constantly putting
her life at risk with all

199
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:11,577
those human pirates coming
and going on the island.

200
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:14,037
We know you're on good
terms with Whitebeard,

201
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:17,577
and to some extent his influence
can protect her while she's there.

202
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:19,580
But anything could happen.

203
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:22,657
That is a fact of which
she is all too aware.

204
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:25,417
And yet it does nothing to deter her.

205
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:31,060
For the world Otohime dreams of
Is far more than a simple fantasy.

206
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:36,937
After all, unifying our peoples was
also the ambition of our ancestors.

207
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:40,797
Although they were never able
to make that vision a reality?

208
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,040
What?

209
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:44,769
I'm afraid that I don't
follow your majesty

210
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:49,117
I can't stop Otohime from
doing what she thinks is right.

211
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:52,037
So it's up to you to keep her safe!

212
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,160
Yes, sir.

213
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:57,620
This Queen Otohime certainly
seemed unique, if nothing else.

214
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:00,217
Sounds like she was a crybaby, too.

215
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:02,065
Did you inherit that from her?

216
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:04,540
Um, yes, I suppose I did.

217
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:07,881
Hold on, you used to be a
soldier for the kingdom?

218
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:12,237
When you grow up in the Fishman District,
where you know nothing but fighting,

219
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,517
there aren't a lot of career
path options available to you.

220
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:17,960
You don't say. That's rough.

221
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,301
Is that where you're from, Hachi?

222
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:23,072
It sounds like a pretty bad neighborhood.

223
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,560
It was.

224
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:26,600
Believe me.

225
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:31,738
Originally, it was an orphanage for
children with no living relatives.

226
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:36,680
But in time, the orphanage became too
much for the administrators to handle.

227
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,260
Before long,

228
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:40,397
it became a lawless area that caught the

229
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:43,068
eye of delinquents from
all over the island.

230
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:47,777
Back then, Fisher Tiger was the
closest thing we had to a leader.

231
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:50,154
but he left to have his own adventures.

232
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:55,380
I'd been his second in command, but
I went on to join Neptune's army.

233
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,180
And despite being fishmen,

234
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:01,697
Macro and some others started
helping the kidnappers.

235
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:03,500
As for everyone else,

236
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:07,460
they all left, following
their own pursuits.

237
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:10,220
Until one day.

238
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,260
Please, give them back!

239
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,540
Oh, you almost had them that time.

240
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:16,637
Hey, knock it off!

241
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,877
Do you realize how hard it was for
her to get all those signatures?

242
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,431
Yeah, and you realize I don't care, right?

243
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:25,080
Hey, cut it out!

244
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,800
You fishman district reject! Huh?

245
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:33,372
You think you're better than
me because of where I'm from?

246
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,220
Let go of me!

247
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,480
You got it backwards, pal.

248
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:44,000
I'm the captain of the Arlong
Pirates, and you're just a nobody.

249
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,821
I clean up all the human
garbage you let run wild.

250
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:51,372
Pirates so pathetic, they can't
even breathe in the water.

251
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:54,640
You guys in Neptune's
army should be faking us.

252
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,391
Maybe I should beat a donation out of you.

253
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,417
Please, I'm in trouble over here.

254
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,080
He's gonna kill me, Boss Jinbei. Jinbei.

255
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:05,620
All right, punk.

256
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:08,394
Just put the rookie down and walk away.

